{"id":44,"text":"A poor woodcutter worked near a river. Every day, he cut wood and sold it in the village. He had only one axe, and it was made of iron.\n\nOne morning, while he was cutting a tree, his axe slipped from his hand and fell into the deep river. “Oh no!” he cried. “How can I work now?” He sat on the ground and began to cry.\n\nSuddenly, a kind spirit came out of the water. “Why are you crying?” it asked.\n\n“I lost my axe,” said the woodcutter.\n\nThe spirit went into the river and came back with a golden axe. “Is this yours?”\n\n“No,” said the woodcutter. “Mine was iron.”\n\nThe spirit brought a silver axe. “Is this yours?”\n\n“No, that is not mine either.”\n\nThe third time, the spirit brought an iron axe. “Yes!” said the woodcutter happily. “This is my axe!”\n\nThe spirit smiled. “You are very honest. Take all three axes as a gift.”\n\nThe woodcutter thanked the spirit and went home. He was happy and rich.\n\nMoral: Honesty is always rewarded.","tr":null,"gl":{"a":"(неопределённый артикль)","poor":"бедный","woodcutter":"дровосек","worked":"работал","near":"рядом","river":"река","every":"каждый","day":"день","he":"он","cut":"резать","wood":"дерево (материал)","and":"и","sold":"продал","it":"оно, это","in":"в","the":"(определённый артикль)","village":"деревня","had":"имел; (прошедшее)","only":"только, единственный","one":"один","axe":"топор","was":"был","made":"сделал","of":"из; (родительный падеж)","iron":"железо","morning":"утро","while":"пока; тогда как","cutting":"резка","tree":"дерево","his":"его","slipped":"поскользнулся","from":"из, от","hand":"рука","fell":"упал","into":"в (внутрь)","deep":"глубокий","oh":"ох","no":"нет; никакой","cried":"заплакал; крикнул","how":"как","can":"мочь","i":"я","work":"работать; работа","now":"сейчас, теперь","sat":"сидел","on":"на","ground":"земля","began":"начал","to":"к, в; чтобы","cry":"плакать","suddenly":"вдруг","kind":"добрый; вид","spirit":"дух","came":"пришёл","out":"наружу","water":"вода; поливать","why":"п